  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Fca Us has $506M in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date from 11,695 awards. Fca Us has an average award size of $43.3K and obligations are up 99.1% year over year. Fca Us obligations show large swings by fiscal year: FY21 $267M, FY22 $16.1M, FY23 $356M, FY24 $330M, FY25 $254M, FY26 $506M. Fca Us current-year totals are partial, covering fiscal year to date, and the reported totals are contract obligations except where award-value figures are explicitly noted as total contract values. Fca Us saw the largest single jump between FY25 and FY26 in the reported series. Fca Us award volume and the average award size together imply a mix of many smaller awards and some larger obligations contributing to the $506M total. Fca Us trends across the six fiscal years show volatility rather than steady growth or decline, with the FY22 low point and FY26 high point framing the recent rise in obligations.",
